          "final_text_tail": "_args(args)`** (new module-level helper, `tool.py:21`):\n   - Recursively sorts dict keys.\n   - Converts tuples to lists (recursing into lists/tuples).\n   - Strips leading/trailing whitespace from string values.\n   - Passes numeric/boolean/other values through unchanged (no type coercion).\n\n3. **`_compute_tool_call_fingerprint(name, args)`** (new helper, `tool.py:40`):\n   - Builds `{\"name\": name, \"args\": _canonicalize_args(args)}`.\n   - Serializes with `json.dumps(..., sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))`.\n   - Returns the SHA-256 hexdigest (64 chars).\n\n4. **`ToolCall` class** (`tool.py:291`):\n   - Added `fingerprint: str = \"\"` and `id: str = \"\"` fields.\n   - Added `model_post_init` (Pydantic's hook that runs during `__init__`) that computes the fingerprint once at creation and sets `id = fingerprint[:8]`.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Comprehensive assertions passed: 64-char fingerprint, 8-char id, deterministic across key-order/whitespace differences, tuple\u2192list equivalence, numeric/bool preservation, name sensitivity, and `from_dict_list` integration.\n- Existing tests all pass: `tests/adapters/test_tool.py` (26 passed), `tests/adapters/test_chat_adapter.py` + `test_json_adapter.py` (42 passed).\n\n**Note:** Ruff reports 6 pre-existing lint errors (an `F811` `Type` redefinition in the imports and `RUF002` en-dashes in the `validate_input` docstring) that exist independent of my changes \u2014 my additions are lint-clean. I left those pre-existing issues untouched as they're out of scope.",
